  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Find your loan size, match it to a band in the table, and ask the bank to confirm the security in writing. Then get one secured and one unsecured quote and compare the rupee gap over the full repayment.
  </p>

  <p><strong>Try it now:</strong> <a href="/tools/course-cost-planner/">Use the free course cost planner</a> to total fees, living cost and loan interest before you borrow.</p>


  <p>
    If the numbers still feel heavy, <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-counselling-for-college-students/">career counselling for college students</a> works through the course, the loan and the skill plan with you. The goal is a debt your family can carry and skills that keep your options open.
  </p>

